    "caption_changes": [
      {
        "before": "Fig. 3 A: scalar TV transfer versus direct MASS-CP on all 1,200 Office-Home candidates. The dashed line denotes equal contrasts; passing risk requires a nonpositive contrast. B: exhaustive one-factor count-state comparisons, 384 pairs per factor. Order changes include ties; none is a strict reversal. These are descriptive finite enumerations",
        "after": "Fig. 3 (a): scalar TV transfer versus direct MASS-CP on all 1,200 Office-Home candidates. The dashed line denotes equal contrasts; passing risk requires a nonpositive contrast. (b): exhaustive one-factor count-state comparisons, 384 pairs per factor. Order changes include ties; none is a strict reversal. These are descriptive finite enumerations"
      },
      {
        "before": "Fig. 5 Cell-wise empirical bound validity on 450 fixed reservoirs. Validity is the fraction of repeated audits in which the reported upper confidence bound covers the exact worst-client conditional risk computed from the complete frozen reservoir. Panel (a) compares Fed-CORE, a conservative clientwise Bonferroni reference, and a pooled negative control. Panel (b) shows 95% Wilson intervals for the 20 lowest apparent Fed-CORE cells after 10,000 audit repetitions",
        "after": "Fig. 5 Cell-wise empirical bound validity on 450 fixed reservoirs. Validity is the fraction of repeated audits in which the reported upper confidence bound covers the exact worst-client conditional risk computed from the complete frozen reservoir. Panel (a) compares Fed-CORE, a conservative clientwise Bonferroni reference, and a pooled negative control. Panels (b) and (c) show 95% Wilson intervals for the 20 lowest apparent Fed-CORE cells after 10,000 audit repetitions"
      },
      {
        "before": "Fig. 9 PathMNIST certification by open-set split and accepted-error target under the theorem-aligned Holm/IUT procedure. Panel (a) shows one deterministic test patch per tissue category. Panel (b) summarizes five repetitions per split and heterogeneity level at \u03b1 = 0.20, colored by effective certified acceptance. Panel (c) shows the accepted-error frontier. All results use one prespecified with-replacement audit per client; clients are synthetic Dirichlet partitions, not hospitals",
        "after": "Fig. 9 PathMNIST certification by open-set split and accepted-error target under the theorem-aligned Holm/IUT procedure. Panel (a) shows one deterministic 28 \u00d7 28-pixel test patch per tissue category. Panel (b) summarizes five repetitions per split and heterogeneity level at \u03b1 = 0.20, colored by effective certified acceptance. Panel (c) shows the accepted-error frontier. All results use one prespecified with-replacement audit per client; clients are synthetic Dirichlet partitions, not hospitals"
      }
    ],
